    {
      "id": "43788528",
      "title": "Managing State & Changing Data",
      "lectureOrder": 27,
      "videoOrder": 23,
      "sourceHash": "c49c8e41866822eb98d55687c50327ae77d7783989900aedd6a6656a89d8a32b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 3.54,
          "en": "Now that we know how we can react to events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.54,
          "end": 7.8,
          "en": "and that we know how we can output dynamic content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.8,
          "end": 11.55,
          "en": "we can bring these two things together,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.55,
          "end": 15.33,
          "en": "as you often will do when building Angular applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.33,
          "end": 17.31,
          "en": "so that we can update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.31,
          "end": 19.41,
          "en": "and what's visible on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.41,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "whenever this user here is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 25.89,
          "en": "so that instead of just outputting something to the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.89,
          "end": 27.9,
          "en": "we update the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.9,
          "end": 30.57,
          "en": "For example, we could change the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.57,
          "end": 33.9,
          "en": "that's displayed here, every time it's clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.9,
          "end": 36.99,
          "en": "so that instead of changing it only when the page reloads,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.99,
          "end": 39.27,
          "en": "we could do that when the user is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.27,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "And for this, we now need to manage some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 43.98,
          "en": "in our component class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.98,
          "end": 48.63,
          "en": "which when changed has an impact on the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.63,
          "end": 52.83,
          "en": "And this kind of data is often also called state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.83,
          "end": 55.44,
          "en": "because it is data that will have an impact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.44,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "on the state of our user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "And setting up and using such state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "is actually pretty straightforward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 65.28,
          "en": "when working with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.28,
          "end": 67.32,
          "en": "Indeed, you actually don't need to set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.32,
          "end": 69.39,
          "en": "anything special at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 72.27,
          "en": "unlike in some other libraries or frameworks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.27,
          "end": 74.58,
          "en": "you could be using instead of Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.58,
          "end": 77.25,
          "en": "instead here in our user component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.25,
          "end": 81.15,
          "en": "we just need to change the value of selected user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.15,
          "end": 84.84,
          "en": "whenever this method down here gets executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.84,
          "end": 87.48,
          "en": "So in this method, instead of console logging,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.48,
          "end": 89.893,
          "en": "we wanna set this selected user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.893,
          "end": 92.553,
          "en": "to a different selected user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.53999999999999,
          "end": 96.03,
          "en": "And for that of course we can copy this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.03,
          "end": 97.68,
          "en": "and paste it in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.68,
          "end": 101.88,
          "en": "but we now also need to make sure that random index changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 104.283,
          "en": "every time this method executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.18,
          "end": 109.11,
          "en": "Because at the moment it's only calculated once, initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.11,
          "end": 113.37,
          "en": "when this file gets passed and never changed thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.37,
          "end": 115.65,
          "en": "So in order to get a new random number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.65,
          "end": 119.25,
          "en": "we can of course simply copy this entire line here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.25,
          "end": 123.03,
          "en": "and paste it into on select user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.03,
          "end": 126.27,
          "en": "so that we generate a new locally scoped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.27,
          "end": 128.13,
          "en": "random index constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.13,
          "end": 131.49,
          "en": "that's only available inside of on select user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.49,
          "end": 135.81,
          "en": "And that overrides this global random index constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.81,
          "end": 138.54,
          "en": "inside of this method here at least.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 140.64,
          "en": "And we then use this random index,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.64,
          "end": 143.94,
          "en": "which is recalculated every time this method runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.94,
          "end": 148.263,
          "en": "to extract and Store a new user from dummy users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.4,
          "end": 152.57999999999998,
          "en": "So the selected user property gets changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.57999999999998,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "every time this method executes now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 156.9,
          "en": "and this method executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.9,
          "end": 159.36,
          "en": "whenever this button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.36,
          "end": 162.12,
          "en": "Therefore, with this simple change made,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.12,
          "end": 164.64,
          "en": "if we now reload and we click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.64,
          "end": 168.75,
          "en": "you see that the users will change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.75,
          "end": 173.64,
          "en": "And that's how easy it is to manage data in Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.64,
          "end": 177.87,
          "en": "which when changed has an impact on the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.87,
          "end": 180.48,
          "en": "You simply change the properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.48,
          "end": 182.85,
          "en": "you are outputting in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.85,
          "end": 184.983,
          "en": "It's as simple as that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
